## Findings (all nonblocking)

F1 [Nit] phase-acceptance: tests/readme/test-readme-heavy-run.sh hides lines from the readme-nothing-else-moves check. Line 219 replaces the whole Guards intro line with a placeholder. Line 235 drops every line that holds the bullet marker or the sentence start. A moved bullet, a moved sentence, a duplicate, or a larger intro rewrite therefore passes. Rationale: FR-1 and FR-2 state where the new sentence and the new bullet go, and FR-5 allows one clause on line 68. The README at 5442514 is correct by diff, so the README holds no wrong text.

F2 [Nit] phase-acceptance: plan.md line 29 gives the diff stat of the range 6cbbe7b..HEAD as 4 files, 321 insertions, and 5 deletions. The same command at the audited HEAD 5442514 prints 5 files, 329 insertions, and 8 deletions. Rationale: the numbers are true for the pushed head f5d2806 only. Pin the range to 6cbbe7b..f5d2806 in the record.

F3 [Nit] phase-acceptance: The Heavy-run guard bullet names the runner prefixes npx and bunx only. The function stripCommand also strips the pair bun x (plugins/opencode-measure-guard/src/core/guards.ts:954). The Checks block of the same README uses that pair. Rationale: the bullet text is true but incomplete. FR-2 has the same wording, so the spec owns the change.

## Proof for F1

I loaded the collapse function (test lines 218 to 236) with eval and fed it README streams from process substitution. These streams gave the hash 5019e172: the real README, the unedited README, an intro cut after the shell tools, a bullet moved to the end, a sentence moved to the end, and a duplicated sentence. An unrelated heading change gave the hash 40304a7a. The function therefore sees real changes but not the changes in F1.

